<Base title="Terms | MinimalPairs" description="Terms for MinimalPairs listening practice, memberships and existing lifetime purchases.">
  <Header /><main class="editorial-wrap"><p class="eyebrow">USING MINIMALPAIRS</p><h1>A clear understanding.</h1><p class="small-note">Updated October 2, 2026</p><section><h2>The listening preview</h2><p>MinimalPairs provides language-listening practice. Examples are curated with stated dialects and references. Errors can occur. Practice scores describe activity in these exercises and are not language certifications or clinical assessments.</p></section><section><h2>Existing purchases</h2><p>Existing lifetime purchases will be honored according to the access promised at purchase, including current and future language trainers where included. This preview does not replace or narrow those purchased rights. A subscription is not required to buy the same access again.</p></section><section><h2>Price and billing</h2><p>The first three exercises per language are free and require no card. New memberships cost $7 USD per month or $49 USD per year and include all available exercises and languages. Payment is collected at checkout; there is no timed trial. Membership renews at the selected interval until canceled. Cancel renewal through your account’s billing settings before your next charge; access continues through the paid period. Cancellation does not automatically issue a refund. Existing paid subscription terms and lifetime coverage are preserved. Your rights under applicable consumer law remain in effect.</p></section><section><h2>Use the service respectfully</h2><p>You may use the exercises for your own learning and ordinary classroom demonstrations. Do not interfere with the service, impersonate another customer or try to obtain someone else's account or purchase access. References remain the property of their respective owners; a reference link does not grant rights to reproduce their material.</p></section><section><h2>Your account and history</h2><p>Keep your sign-in secure. Guest history is stored on your device and may be lost if you clear browser data. You can export it from the account page. We will distinguish account features that are ready from those still being connected.</p></section><section><h2>Questions about an earlier purchase</h2><p>Use the support address on your original MinimalPairs receipt. The rebuilt account flow will explain how to connect a verified account with your purchase.</p></section></main><Footer />
</Base>
